# Project Rules

## General

- Respond in Russian
- Commits: `feature: description` (English)
- Ask confirmation before writing code
- Don't change code just for linter (e.g., quotes)

## Tech Stack

- Backend: Go + Fiber v2 на порту 8080
- Frontend: React 19 + TypeScript + pnpm на порту 5173
- API: OpenAPI-first (спека → генерация кода)

## Code Style

- Don't change code just for linter compliance (e.g., don't change quotes)
- Keep responses concise and to the point
- Ask for confirmation before writing code

## Frontend

- Package manager: pnpm (not npm/yarn)
- Use SCSS Modules for styling (`.module.scss`)
- Regenerate TypeScript client from OpenAPI using `make generate` in `web/` directory
- Follow SOLID principles

### UI Components (`src/ui/`)

**⚠️ Use existing components first. If missing — ask user.**

See available: `src/ui/index.ts`

Icons: `lucide-react` — `import { Search, Heart, Home } from 'lucide-react'`

### Design System (`src/styles/`)

Tokens: `src/styles/_variables.scss` | Mixins: `src/styles/_mixins.scss`

## Backend

- OpenAPI spec: `backend/api/openapi.yaml`
- Generated code: `backend/internal/generated/`
- Regenerate code after changing openapi.yaml using `make generate` in `backend/` directory
- Structure: `cmd/` — entrypoint, `internal/` — business logic
- Follow SOLID principles
- Follow KISS principle
- Always type data and API responses

## Code Generation

- Always use `make generate` commands instead of direct tool calls:
  - Backend: `cd backend && make generate` (generates Go code from OpenAPI)
  - Frontend: `cd web && make generate` (generates TypeScript client from OpenAPI)
- Never call oapi-codegen, openapi-typescript, or other generation tools directly

## Planning

- Use sequential-thinking for complex task planning in agent mode
